WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580
In July 2008, Zimbabwe's official inflation
rate reached 231 million per cent.

2
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.600
By 2009, people there had stopped
using their own currency at all.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.720
Many central banks aim
for something far gentler:

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.610
about 2 per cent a year.

5
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.980
But suppose all pay
rose as fast as prices.

6
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.390
Would inflation still hurt anyone?

7
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.180
In this mission, you'll calculate
inflation rates step by step,

8
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.210
and spot disinflation and deflation.

9
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.100
Then you'll use a graph lab:

10
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.140
two kinds of falling prices,

11
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.270
and what each one does to jobs.

12
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: find out who really
pays the price when prices change.
